WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:03.250
(dreamy dance music)

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.913
- [Narrator] Rising
out of the Tuscan hills

00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:08.010
are some colorful and unusual figures

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.063
inspired by tarot cards.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.120
The Tarot Park is located in Tuscany,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.410
a few hours outside of Rome.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.720
The park took 20 years to complete

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.563
and includes 22 figures
from the tarot deck.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.880
There's a Sphynx that
leads to a golden skeleton

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.710
riding a blue horse over a green sea.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.313
This represents death.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.940
The hanged man can be found inside one

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.850
of the sparkling grottos,
suspended from the ceiling.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.740
And one of the most bizarre figures

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.970
is the Oracle, which
is a hollow-eyed figure

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.423
surrounded and covered by snakes.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.510
The eccentric artist
who created this garden

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.362
was Niki de Saint Phalle.

00:00:58.362 --> 00:01:02.950
In the early 1950s, Niki
was committed to an asylum

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.600
and believes it was art
that eventually healed her.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.480
She wanted to create a
place that would have

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.093
the same healing effect
on those who visited.

00:01:12.341 --> 00:01:14.870
The park opened in 1998,

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.973
just four years before Niki's death.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.110
In her own words, she
dreamt of building a garden

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:24.253
that would be dialog between
sculpture and nature-

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.803
a place to dream in.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.025
(sonic beeping)

